Description: Native hi-fi Qobuz desktop player (Qt6/QML)
 QBZ is a native Qt6/QML Qobuz client for Linux with a focus on
 bit-perfect, hi-res audio playback: DAC passthrough and automatic
 sample-rate switching for each track.
 .
 It plays both your Qobuz subscription and local files, and also talks
 to self-hosted servers (Plex, Jellyfin, Subsonic/Navidrome) through the
 same interface and audio pipeline. No API keys or token extraction; zero
 telemetry, with opt-in scrobbling, metadata enrichment and Discord Rich
 Presence integrations.
 .
 This package also installs qbzd, the headless daemon QBZ's QConnect and
 remote-control features share — see the separate qbzd package if you
 only want the headless/server install with no Qt dependency.

Package: qbzd
Architecture: any
Depends:
  ${shlibs:Depends},
  ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: pipewire, pulseaudio-utils, xdg-utils
Conflicts: qbz
Description: QBZ headless Qobuz playback daemon
 Headless Qobuz playback daemon for servers, Raspberry Pi and other
 appliances — the daemon, its own CLI client, and a setup TUI in one
 binary. No Qt dependency: install this instead of qbz on a box with no
 display, wired straight to a DAC.
 .
 Includes a systemd user unit (shipped disabled — see
 /usr/share/doc/qbzd/README.md, in particular the `loginctl
 enable-linger` requirement for headless boxes) and can generate service
 definitions for systemd, OpenRC or runit via its own CLI.
